WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.536
This workshop connects five school reading rows to the same Week Two patients. The detailed paired English and Chinese reading below expands the chapter domains and every saved assigned BCPEG page, rather than asking you to infer the lesson from a few headings.
本研习把5项学校阅读连接到同一组第2周患者。下方逐段中英阅读扩展章节领域，并涵盖存档BCPEG全部指定页，不让你仅凭几个标题自行猜出课程。

00:00:16.536 --> 00:00:30.240
Chemistry explains concentrations and acid-base changes; autonomic physiology explains receptor effects; pressure physiology and vital-sign integration explain why the response must be checked in the patient.
化学解释浓度及酸碱变化，自主神经生理解释受体作用，血压生理与体征整合则解释为什么必须从患者身上核实反应。

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:42.576
Use the reading index to open the book-specific bilingual guide after the lecture. It includes definitions, mechanisms, clinical links, source corrections and original retrieval tasks.
听讲后可通过阅读目录打开对应教材双语讲解，内含定义、机制、临床联系、来源修正及原创提取任务。

00:00:42.576 --> 00:00:59.040
The remaining school book rows, exact school exports and some interactive content are still separate work, not declared complete by this workshop. Source boundaries are visible so that the presence of a reading button cannot be mistaken for full-week completion.
其他学校教材行、准确学校导出本及部分互动内容仍是独立待办，不会因为这堂研习就宣布完成。来源边界保持可见，避免把有一个阅读按钮误当整周完成。

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:10.296
Moodle Week Two links five supplemental articles. Their original English-Chinese guides are in the reading index; these slides do not reproduce the articles or their cases.
Moodle第2周另链接五篇补充文章。阅读目录提供原创中英讲解；本课件不复制文章原文或案例。

00:01:10.296 --> 00:01:22.968
The overdose article teaches a respiratory emergency, but it dates from 2013. Support ventilation first; use the current BCEHS pathway for medication and follow-up decisions.
过量文章讲的是呼吸急症，但发表于2013年。先支持通气；药物及后续决定应查现行BCEHS路径。

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:35.520
The pain and nitrous articles prompt patient-centred assessment, self-administration limits, non-drug relief and reassessment. They are not local product instructions or permission to administer.
疼痛及一氧化二氮文章引导以患者为中心评估、自我给药限制、非药物缓解及复评，但不是本地产品说明或给药授权。

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:49.896
Bariatric airway and cough cases remind you to plan for reduced reserve, positioning, ventilation, transport and competing causes. Do not diagnose from one sign or import old dosing formulas.
肥胖气道及咳嗽案例提醒你计划较低储备、体位、通气、转运及多种病因。不能凭一个体征诊断，也不能照搬旧剂量公式。

00:01:49.896 --> 00:02:02.736
For any real intervention, use the current service guideline, exact device instructions, licence level and training. Historical links are discussion material, not a substitute for those controls.
任何真实干预都要依据现行服务指引、确切设备说明、执照级别及培训。历史链接只是讨论材料，不能取代这些控制。

00:02:02.736 --> 00:02:15.432
An amount tells how much substance is present. A concentration tells how much of it is present in a specified amount of mixture or solution. Neither number is useful until its units are named.
药量说明有多少物质，浓度说明特定量混合物或溶液中有多少物质；不说单位，这两个数字都没有明确用途。

00:02:15.432 --> 00:02:29.064
For a fictional two milligrams in a final ten millilitres, the concentration is zero point two milligrams per millilitre. Ten millilitres is the final solution, not automatically the amount of diluent added.
虚构2毫克配至最终10毫升，浓度为每毫升0.2毫克。10毫升是最终溶液，不自动等于加入的稀释液量。

00:02:29.064 --> 00:02:41.016
An amount of one milligram would therefore require five millilitres. The result still needs route, maximum, rate, patient and device checks before any real administration.
因此需要1毫克时，体积为5毫升；真实给药前仍须核途径、上限、速度、患者及装置。

00:02:41.016 --> 00:02:55.536
Chemistry also uses moles per litre, while Canadian glucose records commonly use millimoles per litre. Do not turn a glucose concentration into a drug volume by cancelling unlike substances or unrelated units.
化学还使用摩尔每升，加拿大血糖常用毫摩尔每升。不能拿不同物质或无关单位相约，把血糖浓度直接算成某种药液体积。

00:02:55.536 --> 00:03:06.672
An element is identified by its number of protons. Change the neutron number and you have an isotope; change the electron balance and you have an ion, not a new element.
元素由质子数确定。改变中子数得到同位素，改变电子平衡得到离子，而不是新元素。

00:03:06.672 --> 00:03:20.928
Sodium and potassium ions help create electrical gradients across cell membranes. An ECG records the combined electrical activity of heart tissue; it is not a direct measurement of the blood potassium concentration.
钠与钾离子帮助形成细胞膜两侧电梯度。ECG记录心脏组织合成电活动，不是直接测血钾浓度。

00:03:20.928 --> 00:03:31.584
Ionic charge is not a dose, and a radioisotope half-life is not a drug elimination half-life. Similar-looking terms can describe different physical processes.
离子电荷不是剂量，放射性同位素半衰期也不是药物消除半衰期。外观相似的术语可能描述完全不同过程。

00:03:31.584 --> 00:03:42.624
For the exam, be able to distinguish those terms before applying them. A correct definition becomes useful when you can say what it does and does not tell you about the patient.
备考时应先能区分这些术语，再应用。正确的定义只有在你能说明它告诉或不能告诉我们患者什么时，才真正有用。

00:03:42.624 --> 00:03:55.104
Sodium chloride separates into ions in water, while a glucose molecule can dissolve without separating into sodium-like ions. Dissolving and ionic dissociation are not the same statement.
氯化钠在水中解离为离子，葡萄糖分子则能溶解而不变成类似钠那样的离子。溶解与离子解离不是同一句话。

00:03:55.104 --> 00:04:09.048
Polar water interacts well with many charged or polar groups. Nonpolar regions behave differently, helping explain the organization of phospholipid membranes and why formulation matters to drug delivery.
极性水与许多带电或极性基团相互作用良好，非极性区域则不同；这有助解释磷脂膜组织方式，以及剂型为何影响药物送入。

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:21.768
Proteins have specific three-dimensional shapes and chemical binding environments. A drug does not produce an effect merely by existing somewhere in the body; it needs the appropriate target interaction.
蛋白具有特定三维形状及化学结合环境。药物不会仅因存在于体内某处就自动产生效果，还需要适当靶点相互作用。

00:04:21.768 --> 00:04:37.368
The detailed reading names all four organic groups and the relevant structural vocabulary. Connect the molecular definition to a membrane, enzyme, receptor or energy process instead of memorizing a disconnected spelling list.
详细阅读列出四类有机物及相关结构词汇。应把分子定义连到膜、酶、受体或能量过程，不能只背一份互不相连的拼写表。

00:04:37.368 --> 00:04:52.512
A chemical reaction changes which atoms are joined and how the products are arranged. Breaking bonds requires energy, while forming bonds releases energy; the net reaction decides whether useful energy is released.
化学反应改变原子的连接及产物排列。断键需要能量、成键释放能量，整个反应的净变化决定是否释放可用能量。

00:04:52.512 --> 00:05:05.592
Enzymes lower activation energy and improve reaction rate under suitable conditions. They do not create energy or erase the difference between an energetically favourable and unfavourable reaction.
酶降低活化能，在适当条件下提高反应速度，但不创造能量，也不会抹去有利与不利反应的差别。

00:05:05.592 --> 00:05:19.008
ATP hydrolysis can be coupled to membrane pumps, muscle contraction and synthesis. Think of the full reaction and the coupled work, not a magical energy packet released by any bond breaking.
ATP水解可与膜泵、肌肉收缩及合成偶联。应想到完整反应及偶联工作，不能把任何断键都想成释放神奇能量包。

00:05:19.008 --> 00:05:32.664
This explains why oxygen delivery and substrate availability matter but are not sufficient by themselves. The cells also need functioning enzymes, membranes and circulation to sustain useful metabolism.
这解释了氧输送及底物可用性为何重要，却不能单独保证正常代谢；细胞还需要有效酶、膜及循环来维持有用代谢。

00:05:32.664 --> 00:05:45.360
Carbon dioxide is linked to water, carbonic acid, hydrogen ions and bicarbonate through a reversible system. Removing carbon dioxide is therefore part of maintaining acid-base balance.
二氧化碳通过可逆系统与水、碳酸、氢离子及碳酸氢根联系，因此排出二氧化碳是维持酸碱平衡的一部分。

00:05:45.360 --> 00:06:00.576
At otherwise comparable conditions, inadequate alveolar ventilation retains carbon dioxide and tends toward respiratory acidosis. A normal oxygen saturation on supplemental oxygen does not cancel that problem.
其他条件相近时，肺泡通气不足使二氧化碳潴留，并趋向呼吸性酸中毒。补氧后血氧正常，也不能取消这个问题。

00:06:00.576 --> 00:06:11.328
Rapid breathing can instead be compensation for a metabolic acid load. Labeling it anxiety and suppressing it without assessing the cause can remove a useful compensation.
快速呼吸反而可能是在代偿代谢性酸负荷。未评估原因就标为焦虑并抑制它，可能去掉有用代偿。

00:06:11.328 --> 00:06:26.256
The end-tidal value is influenced by ventilation, perfusion, dead space and sampling. Use it with the patient and the complete situation; do not announce a full acid-base diagnosis from one displayed value.
呼气末值受通气、灌注、死腔及采样影响，应与患者及完整情境一起解释，不能靠一个显示值就宣布完整酸碱诊断。

00:06:26.256 --> 00:06:39.504
Glucose and glycogen are not interchangeable names: one is a monosaccharide and the other a storage polymer. The available fuel and its location matter when interpreting a glucose emergency.
葡萄糖与糖原不是可互换名称，前者是单糖，后者是储存聚合物。解释血糖急症时，要看可用燃料及其所在位置。

00:06:39.504 --> 00:06:51.216
Lipids include energy-rich triglycerides and amphipathic phospholipids that form membranes. Steroid precursors and signalling lipids have roles beyond storing calories.
脂质包括高能甘油三酯及形成膜的双亲性磷脂，类固醇前体及信号脂质的作用不止储存热量。

00:06:51.216 --> 00:07:05.304
Protein shape supports a specific function: an antibody, an enzyme and a receptor do not perform the same task merely because they are all proteins. Binding and denaturation depend on that structure.
蛋白形状支持特定功能。抗体、酶及受体不会仅因都属蛋白就执行相同任务，结合与变性取决于其结构。

00:07:05.304 --> 00:07:21.456
DNA and RNA are polymers made from nucleotides, whereas ATP is a nucleotide used in energy coupling. Read the detailed section for their components, then explain how a receptor protein and ATP-dependent pump connect these categories.
DNA及RNA是核苷酸聚合物，ATP则是用于能量偶联的核苷酸。读详细组分后，应能解释受体蛋白及ATP依赖泵如何把这些类别联系起来。

00:07:21.456 --> 00:07:34.056
Autonomic motor pathways generally use a neuron from the central nervous system to a ganglion, then a neuron from that ganglion to the organ. Name both the transmitter and the receptor at each connection.
自主运动通路通常由中枢神经元至神经节，再由神经节神经元至器官。每一连接都应同时说出递质与受体。

00:07:34.056 --> 00:07:48.888
Both divisions use acetylcholine at nicotinic ganglion receptors. Parasympathetic organ targets generally use muscarinic receptors, while most sympathetic organ targets receive norepinephrine at adrenergic receptors.
两系统都以乙酰胆碱作用于神经节烟碱型受体；副交感器官靶点通常为毒蕈碱型，多数交感器官靶点则接受去甲肾上腺素作用于肾上腺素能受体。

00:07:48.888 --> 00:08:00.336
Eccrine sweat glands are an important sympathetic cholinergic exception. This is why acetylcholine cannot simply be translated as parasympathetic in every sentence.
小汗腺是重要的胆碱能交感例外，所以不能在所有句子里直接把“乙酰胆碱”翻译成“副交感”。

00:08:00.336 --> 00:08:14.400
The adrenal medulla is a related endocrine branch that releases catecholamines into blood. The diagram is a signal map, not a promise that every autonomic action uses an identical anatomical distance or circuit.
肾上腺髓质是相关内分泌分支，可向血液释放儿茶酚胺。本图是信号图，不代表所有自主作用都使用相同解剖距离或回路。

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:25.032
The same broad chemical family can increase cardiac activity, constrict some vessels and relax bronchial smooth muscle because the target receptors and their signalling differ.
同一大类化学信号可以增加心脏活动、使部分血管收缩并舒张支气管平滑肌，因为靶受体及其信号不同。

00:08:25.032 --> 00:08:36.744
Use alpha one for the key vascular constrictor association, beta one for important cardiac rate and force effects, and beta two for the bronchodilator association relevant this week.
本周应掌握α1的重要缩血管联系、β1的重要心率与收缩力联系，以及β2扩支气管联系。

00:08:36.744 --> 00:08:47.856
Muscarinic effects also depend on the tissue and subtype. Reducing a vagal effect on a node is not the same action as directly stimulating every adrenergic receptor in the body.
毒蕈碱作用也取决于组织及亚型。减少结点上的迷走影响，不等于直接激动全身每一种肾上腺素能受体。

00:08:47.856 --> 00:09:00.408
Receptor selectivity is not absolute isolation. A selected bronchodilator can still cause tremor or tachycardia, so the expected benefit and relevant harms must both be reassessed.
受体选择性不是绝对隔离。所选扩支气管药仍可能引起震颤或心动过速，因此预期益处及相关伤害都须复评。

00:09:00.408 --> 00:09:15.240
After salbutamol, look for easier airflow, less work and improved speech, while checking adverse cardiac effects and the actual inhaled delivery. Do not measure success only by whether the inhaler was emptied.
沙丁胺醇后应看气流更易、呼吸功减少及说话改善，同时查心脏不良效应及真实吸入给入。不能仅以吸入器是否喷完判断成功。

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:27.096
Ipratropium reduces bronchial muscarinic effects and is paired with salbutamol under the indicated severe-bronchospasm plan. Their mechanisms differ even when they are administered together.
异丙托溴铵减少支气管毒蕈碱作用，并在有适应证的严重痉挛方案中配沙丁胺醇。即使一起给，两者机制也不同。

00:09:27.096 --> 00:09:38.280
Epinephrine acts at several alpha and beta targets. That does not make every route or advanced-care dose appropriate for a PCP anaphylaxis or bronchospasm scenario.
肾上腺素作用于多个α及β靶点，但不代表任何途径或高级照护剂量，都适合PCP全身过敏或痉挛情境。

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:51.600
Naloxone belongs on a different receptor map: it antagonizes opioid effects. Its relevant endpoint is adequate ventilation, and it must not distract the crew from opening and supporting the airway.
纳洛酮属于另一受体图，拮抗阿片作用。相关终点是足够通气，不能让它转移团队开放及支持气道的注意力。

00:09:51.600 --> 00:10:03.480
A reflex has an input, integration and output, not merely a symptom. Arterial stretch signals help brainstem circuits adjust autonomic output to the heart and vessels.
反射包含输入、整合及输出，不只是某个症状。动脉牵张信号帮助脑干回路调整对心脏及血管的自主传出。

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:17.232
When pressure or effective circulating volume falls, increased sympathetic effects may help maintain perfusion. A beta blocker, autonomic disease or severe deterioration can alter the expected pulse response.
压力或有效循环量下降时，交感效应增加可能帮助维持灌注。β阻断药、自主神经疾病或严重恶化，都可改变预期脉搏反应。

00:10:17.232 --> 00:10:29.088
Most systemic vessels do not have equal opposing parasympathetic control. A lower sympathetic constrictor drive can produce dilation without inventing a new parasympathetic impulse.
多数体循环血管没有等量相反的副交感控制。交感缩血管驱动减少即可舒张，不必假设出现了新的副交感冲动。

00:10:29.088 --> 00:10:45.120
Long reflexes involve the central nervous system; short enteric reflexes can integrate locally. These distinctions help you understand regulation, but a theoretical reflex diagram does not replace actual blood pressure and perfusion checks.
长反射涉及中枢，短肠神经反射可局部整合。这些区分有助理解调节，但理论反射图不能代替真实血压及灌注检查。

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:57.408
Light input reaches a pretectal relay and bilateral parasympathetic output through the Edinger-Westphal system. That bilateral connection helps explain direct and consensual constriction.
光输入到达顶盖前区中继，再经Edinger-Westphal系统连接双侧副交感输出。这种双侧连接有助解释直接及间接缩瞳。

00:10:57.408 --> 00:11:07.488
The efferent constrictor pathway travels with cranial nerve three through the ciliary ganglion to the iris sphincter. Dilation uses a different sympathetic pathway.
缩瞳传出随III脑神经，经睫状神经节至虹膜括约肌；散瞳使用另一交感通路。

00:11:07.488 --> 00:11:18.552
The candidate chapter simplifies this into a hypothalamic relay. The bilingual guide corrects that pathway without pretending that one pupil sign can locate every lesion.
候选章节把它简化成下丘脑中继，双语讲解已修正，但不会假装单一瞳孔征象能定位所有病变。

00:11:18.552 --> 00:11:32.952
Check pupil size, symmetry and reaction with the light conditions, eye history, medication and the rest of the examination. Pinpoint pupils support an opioid hypothesis but do not replace a respiratory assessment.
瞳孔大小、对称及反应应结合光照、眼病史、药物及其余检查。针尖样瞳孔支持阿片假设，但不能代替呼吸评估。

00:11:32.952 --> 00:11:46.560
Pressure reflects an interaction between output and resistance, while useful tissue delivery also depends on circulation and oxygen content. A high cuff value alone cannot prove adequate forward flow.
血压反映输出及阻力交互，而有效组织输送还依赖循环及含氧量。一次袖带高值不能单独证明向前血流足够。

00:11:46.560 --> 00:12:01.704
Primary hypertension is multifactorial. Secondary hypertension has an underlying cause such as renal, endocrine, vascular or medication disease; neither a young age nor one urine result decides the distinction.
原发高血压为多因素，继发则有肾、内分泌、血管或药物等底层原因。年轻年龄或一次尿检，都不能单独决定分类。

00:12:01.704 --> 00:12:15.720
Sustained high afterload can increase ventricular work and oxygen demand, impair filling or ejection and contribute to heart failure. Vascular injury can affect brain, kidneys, eyes and the aorta.
持续高后负荷可增加心室工作及耗氧，损害充盈或射血，并促心衰；血管损伤则可累及脑、肾、眼及主动脉。

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:28.152
Use that mechanism to understand the history and complications, not to prescribe rapid pressure reduction from a textbook graph. The next question is whether there is an acute dangerous syndrome now.
应以机制理解病史及并发症，不能从教材图直接开快速降压方案。下一问题是现在是否存在急性危险综合征。

00:12:28.152 --> 00:12:40.776
Severe pressure with acute target-organ injury or an important acute syndrome differs from an isolated asymptomatic reading. Both require an appropriate plan, but not the same immediate treatment.
严重高压伴急性靶器官损伤或重要急性综合征，与孤立无症状读数不同。两者都需适当计划，但不代表应立即使用同一治疗。

00:12:40.776 --> 00:12:54.384
Assess new neurologic findings, chest pain, severe dyspnea, awareness and other relevant concerns. A high pressure can be part of the problem, a response to it or a coincidental chronic condition.
应评估新神经发现、胸痛、严重呼吸困难、意识及其他相关危险。高压可能是问题一部分、对问题的反应，或并存慢性状态。

00:12:54.384 --> 00:13:06.792
Verify measurement when safe and communicate the baseline, symptoms, medicines and trend. Do not delay airway support while repeatedly measuring a pressure that is already clinically concerning.
安全时核实测量，并报告基线、症状、药物及趋势。血压已提示临床危险时，不能因反复测量而耽误气道支持。

00:13:06.792 --> 00:13:20.424
Do not give extra home antihypertensives or try to make every number normal rapidly. Chronic primary-care targets, acute stroke and pregnancy emergencies follow different clinical pathways and authority.
不能额外给家用降压药，也不能企图迅速把所有数字降到正常。慢性基层目标、急性卒中及妊娠急症，适用不同临床路径及权限。

00:13:20.424 --> 00:13:35.304
The school focus names naloxone, salbutamol and epinephrine, but pages sixty-six through seventy-seven include more. The bilingual reading includes every named product in that actual page span, not only the focus keywords.
学校重点点名纳洛酮、沙丁胺醇及肾上腺素，但66至77页包含更多。双语阅读覆盖实际页段中每一种具名药，不只覆盖重点关键词。

00:13:35.304 --> 00:13:49.368
Use the same worksheet for each: class and mechanism, actual indication, exclusions, amount and maximum, route and concentration, timing, adverse effects and required reassessment.
每种药均使用同一工作表：分类机制、真实适应证、排除、药量及上限、途径浓度、时间、不良反应及所需复评。

00:13:49.368 --> 00:14:01.272
Then add prior doses and consultation or training conditions. A correct amount taken from a page is not permission to use that medicine for an unrelated symptom or by a different route.
再补前剂、咨询或训练条件。从某页抄到正确药量，不代表可以为无关症状或换个途径使用。

00:14:01.272 --> 00:14:13.200
Some saved entries differ materially from current service guidance. Learn the named examination statement and the current difference as separate evidence, not a homemade hybrid regimen.
有些存档条目与当前服务指引存在实质差异。应把具名考试表述与当前差异作为分开的证据学习，不能拼成自制混合方案。

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:26.280
Examples include glucagon route and repeat consultation, the ibuprofen pediatric fever schedule, the ondansetron age boundary and nitroglycerin repeat requirements. These are not cosmetic differences.
例子包括胰高血糖素途径及重复前咨询、布洛芬儿科退热方案、昂丹司琼年龄边界，以及硝酸甘油重复要求。这些都不是排版差异。

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:38.208
Record the source title, date and exact conflicting point. Never solve the problem by taking the dose from one version, interval from another and permission from a general textbook.
应记录来源标题、日期及准确冲突点。绝不能从一版取药量、另一版取间隔，再从普通教材取权限来“解决”。

00:14:38.208 --> 00:14:52.704
Bring the conflict to the instructor before the official station or exam, while using the actual current authorized pathway in clinical practice. The package must not invent an answer to a school-version question it cannot verify.
正式训练站或考试前，应请教师确认冲突；临床实践则使用真实现行获准路径。材料不能为尚未核实的学校版本问题编答案。

00:14:52.704 --> 00:15:05.112
The source panel and bilingual reading retain those differences. An honest unresolved item is safer and more useful than an authoritative-looking slide that silently changes its source.
来源面板及双语阅读保留这些差异。诚实注明未解决项，比看似权威却悄悄改变来源的幻灯更安全、更有用。

00:15:05.112 --> 00:15:18.144
The Week 2 directed list assigns Anatomy and Physiology 2e section 6.5, page 815. We checked the exact course-folder PDF rather than guessing from a different edition.
第2周技能阅读清单指定《Anatomy and Physiology》第2版6.5节第815页。我们核对了准确课程文件，而不是用别的版次猜页码。

00:15:18.144 --> 00:15:39.744
In that course copy, section 6.5, “Fractures: Bone Repair,” is on printed pages 212 to 214, physical PDF pages 228 to 230. The exact page 815 is in section 20.1, “Structure and Function of Blood Vessels.”
该课程版本中，6.5节“骨折：骨修复”在印刷页212至214，即PDF物理页228至230。准确的第815页属于20.1节“血管的结构与功能”。

00:15:39.744 --> 00:15:57.312
The verified fracture section explains that fat globules released from a femoral shaft fracture may travel to and lodge in pulmonary capillary beds, causing respiratory distress. This is the assigned clinical connection, but the school’s printed locator needs instructor clarification.
已核实的骨折章节解释，股骨干骨折释放的脂肪滴可能进入并停留于肺毛细血管床，引发呼吸窘迫。这是指定的临床联系，但学校印刷页码仍需教师澄清。

00:15:57.312 --> 00:16:13.512
For the learner, the actionable lesson is to reassess the whole patient and respond to new respiratory or neurologic deterioration through the current pathway. Do not diagnose fat embolism from one sign or treat this reading as a field protocol.
对学习者的实际启示是持续复评整体患者，并按现行路径处理新发呼吸或神经恶化。不能凭一个体征诊断脂肪栓塞，也不能把这段阅读当现场处置规程。

00:16:13.512 --> 00:16:25.608
Vital-sign integration means looking at the relationship between measurements and the person. An initially fast rate can fall because treatment helped or because the patient is becoming exhausted.
体征整合是看测量与患者的关系。起初很快的呼吸，可能因治疗有效而变慢，也可能因疲劳衰竭而变慢。

00:16:25.608 --> 00:16:37.440
In this original trend, the rate falls to eighteen but breaths become barely visible, the person becomes drowsy and pressure falls. Those findings do not describe recovery.
本原创趋势中，频率降至18，但呼吸几乎不可见、患者嗜睡且血压下降。这些发现不代表恢复。

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:51.192
Reassess and support airway, ventilation and circulation now. Confirm the measurement and equipment without dismissing the patient's deterioration as artifact merely because one number looks normal.
应立即重评并支持气道、通气及循环。核实测量与器械时，不能因为一个数字正常，就把患者恶化一概说成伪差。

00:16:51.192 --> 00:17:06.240
Record time, device, oxygen flow, body position and associated findings so that the receiver can interpret the trend. Good documentation preserves the comparison rather than averaging away its most important change.
应记录时间、装置、氧流、体位及伴随发现，使接收者能解释趋势。好记录保留比较，而不是以平均数抹掉最重要的变化。

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:46.512
Read the May 2026 BCEHS CPAP card as paired columns, not equal numbers. Oxygen flows of 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10 L/min correspond on that card to pressures of 5, 6, 7.5, 10, 12.5 and 15 cmH2O. Its treatment cap remains 10 cmH2O: in the displayed baseline table, that is 8 L/min, not 10 L/min. Check the actual pressure gauge and device configuration; this is a named service-card table, not a universal equation for every CPAP system.
读2026年5月BCEHS CPAP卡时，应按成对列对应，不把流量和压力视为相同数字。卡片氧流量5、6、7、8、9、10L/min，分别对应压力5、6、7.5、10、12.5、15厘米水柱。治疗上限仍为10厘米水柱；在显示的基本表中，对应的是8L/min，不是10L/min。须核实际压力表及装置配置；这是具名服务卡的表，不是所有CPAP系统的通用公式。

00:17:46.512 --> 00:18:26.256
Connect the ports by function on the May 2026 card: red is supplemental oxygen, green is the nebulizer-tubing connection, and black ports are marked for no prehospital use. The pressure gauge measures pressure, not oxygen concentration. The card starts at 5 L/min and says an attached T-piece nebulizer configuration needs 7 L/min extra flow; the prose instead says 7-8. Preserve that difference and follow the trained configuration while monitoring pressure, rather than adding flow indiscriminately or treating an auxiliary connection as the baseline pressure circuit.
2026年5月卡片按功能区分端口：红色是补充氧气，绿色连接雾化器管路，黑色标为不作院前使用。压力表测压力，不测氧浓度。卡片从5L/min开始，并写连接T形雾化配置时增加7L/min；正文则写增加7至8。须保留差异，按受训配置并监测压力操作，不能不加区别地加流量，也不能把辅助连接当作基本压力回路。

00:18:26.256 --> 00:19:02.256
A nasal medicine is absorbed through nasal mucosa; the patient does not need to inhale it into the lungs. J12 still says intranasal uptake requires ongoing respirations, but the manufacturer explicitly states that a person need not be breathing for its sealed NARCAN spray to work. Do not turn that source wording into a reason to withhold an otherwise indicated authorized nasal product in apnea. Continue effective ventilation in parallel; product-specific instructions and current service authority still govern route and dosing.
鼻内药物通过鼻黏膜吸收，不需要患者把药吸进肺。J12仍写鼻内吸收需要持续呼吸，但制造商明确指出，使用其密封NARCAN鼻喷并不要求患者正在呼吸。不能把该来源措辞变成对呼吸暂停者扣住其他方面有适应证、且获授权鼻喷的理由。与此同时仍须有效通气；具体制剂说明及现行服务权限继续决定途径和剂量。

00:19:02.256 --> 00:19:36.696
PR11 limits delivered volume to 1 mL per nostril; if the volume is too large, reconsider the route rather than pushing excess fluid into the nose. A sealed single-dose nasal spray is used according to its own instructions: do not open, dilute, prime, divide or add atomizer dead space merely because a syringe technique was taught nearby. Reassess the clinical effect and document product, amount, route, time and response; a route change does not change the intended patient endpoint.
PR11限制每侧鼻孔给入体积1毫升；所需体积过大时应重新考虑途径，不把多余液体强推入鼻。密封单剂量鼻喷须按自己的说明使用，不能因旁边学过注射器技术，就拆开、稀释、预喷、分剂或增加雾化器死腔。复评临床效果，并记录制剂、药量、途径、时间及反应；换途径不改变患者的预定终点。

00:19:36.696 --> 00:20:20.976
The literal page-371 boundary introduces button batteries, although the school names J12 rather than J13. A battery lodged in the esophagus can cause serious injury without obvious symptoms. Larger 20-25-mm lithium cells and young children are prominent source risk contexts, but a smaller cell or quiet appearance cannot rule out danger. Ask about missing batteries/devices and ingestion timing; nausea, pain, cough, feeding difficulty or unusual noisy breathing may be nonspecific clues. Assess the airway promptly, do not induce vomiting and do not delay emergency-department conveyance to find honey.
字面371页引入纽扣电池，虽然学校点名的是J12而非J13。电池卡在食管，即使没有明显症状也可造成严重损伤。较大20至25毫米锂电池及幼儿是来源重点风险背景，但较小电池或安静外观都不能排除危险。询问丢失的电池或装置及吞入时间；恶心、疼痛、咳嗽、进食困难或异常呼吸声可能只是非特异线索。及时评气道，不催吐，不为找蜂蜜延误送急诊。

00:20:20.976 --> 00:21:00.720
Battery chemistry connects this endpoint to the assigned A&P chapter. Tissue fluid completes an electrical circuit, producing hydroxide ions and an alkaline burn, especially near the negative pole. The J13 opening incorrectly uses radical/coagulative-necrosis wording; its own later body instead describes liquefactive necrosis, consistent with an alkaline injury. This is not simply pressure from a coin-shaped object. Honey is only a conditional measure under the complete appropriate pathway, never a substitute for urgent removal or a blanket oral treatment for an unsafe airway.
电池化学把这一页末连接到指定A&P章节。组织液闭合电路，产生氢氧根离子及碱性灼伤，负极附近尤其明显。J13开头错误使用自由基及凝固性坏死措辞，而它自己的后文改为液化性坏死，与碱性损伤一致。这不只是硬币形物体的压力问题。蜂蜜仅是完整适用路径下的有条件措施，不代替紧急取出，也不是给不安全气道一律口服的处理。

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:13.248
An adult with wheeze becomes fatigued and has a history of beta-blocker use. A medication name alone cannot tell you whether ventilation is adequate or whether the airway diagnosis is complete.
一位哮鸣成人逐渐疲劳，且有使用β阻断药史。仅一个药名，不能告诉你通气是否足够，或气道诊断是否完整。

00:21:13.248 --> 00:21:26.760
Explain why the actual bronchospasm findings support the selected treatment, how the device delivers it and what effect you expect from the receptor mechanism. Check the real contraindications and prior exposure.
应解释真实痉挛发现为何支持所选治疗、装置如何送入、受体机制预期什么效果，并核真实禁忌及前次暴露。

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:39.936
Observe air entry, work and speech as well as pulse and oxygenation. Consider whether the patient can actually use the interface; counting sprays is not a substitute for delivered treatment.
除脉搏及氧合外，还应观察气流、呼吸功及说话；考虑患者能否真正使用界面，计喷数不能代替实际送入。

00:21:39.936 --> 00:21:53.400
If breathing becomes ineffective, support it while reconsidering the cause and obtaining help. Chemistry and receptor knowledge should improve the decision, not distract you from a patient who needs a breath.
若呼吸变无效，应支持呼吸，同时重新考虑原因并求援。化学及受体知识应该改善决定，不能让你忽略一个需要通气的患者。

00:21:53.400 --> 00:22:06.408
First define amount, concentration, ion, buffer, agonist and antagonist without looking. Then give one example of how confusing two terms could cause a clinical error.
先不看资料定义药量、浓度、离子、缓冲、激动药及拮抗药，再举出混淆其中两个术语如何造成临床错误。

00:22:06.408 --> 00:22:18.312
Trace both autonomic pathways and explain why acetylcholine is not always parasympathetic. Predict an important effect and adverse effect for the respiratory drugs assigned this week.
追踪两条自主神经通路，解释乙酰胆碱为何不总等于副交感，并预测本周呼吸药的一项重要作用及不良效应。

00:22:18.312 --> 00:22:31.896
Explain why oxygen saturation can improve while ventilation fails, why high blood pressure does not prove good tissue flow and why an indication-specific route can override a generic fastest-route ranking.
解释为何血氧改善时通气仍可失败、高血压为何不证明组织血流良好，以及具体适应证途径为何可优先于笼统“最快途径”排名。

00:22:31.896 --> 00:22:46.368
Finally use the reading index to review the detailed book sections, then answer the original practice before opening its reasoning. Keep unresolved school pages and activities on the coverage list instead of marking them done by memory.
最后通过阅读目录复习详细教材分节，再先答原创练习后看解析。尚未解决的学校页段及活动应留在覆盖清单，不能靠印象标完成。
